menu "ISA-dependent Options for riscv"

config RV64
  bool "64-bit RISC-V architecture"
  default n

config RV_ASID_BITS
  int "Implemented RV64 satp ASID bits"
  depends on RV64
  range 0 16
  default 16
  help
    Generic RV64 platforms implement all 16 ASID bits, matching Sail.
    Set to 9 for the Raptor reference model. Unimplemented high ASID
    bits read as zero; MODE and PPN retain their existing WARL behavior.

config RV_PMPADDR_BITS
  int "Implemented RV64 pmpaddr bits"
  depends on RV64
  range 1 54
  default 54
  help
    pmpaddr holds physical-address bits [N+1:2]. The architectural maximum
    for RV64 is 54 (56-bit physical addresses). Set to 30 for the Raptor
    reference model, whose RTL implements 32 physical-address bits
    (RAPT_PADDR_BITS). Configurable Raptor references use 30..36
    for PA 32..38. Unimplemented high bits read as zero.

config RV_PC_BITS
  int "Implemented RV64 PC bits"
  depends on RV64
  range 40 64
  default 64
  help
    Width of the implemented PC representation. With 40, a jump, xRET or
    trap-vector target whose bits [63:39] are not all equal is replaced by
    another invalid address before it becomes the PC: bits [37:0] are kept,
    bit 38 becomes the inverse of bit 63 and bits [63:39] copy bit 63. This
    matches Raptor RTL with RAPT_PADDR_BITS <= 39 (the privileged spec lets
    xepc/xtval hold a converted invalid address). Keep 64 for other targets.

config RV_PMP_GRANULARITY_LOG2
  int "PMP minimum region size (log2 bytes)"
  range 2 12
  default 12
  help
    Raptor implements 4 KiB PMP regions (12, architectural G=10).
    NA4 is unavailable above 2. OFF/TOR addresses read with G low
    bits cleared; NAPOT addresses read with G-1 low bits set, while
    retaining the underlying stored address across mode changes.
    Set to 2 for comparison with the legacy 4-byte-grain platform.

config RVE
  bool "Use E extension"
  default n

config RV_F
  bool "F: single-precision floating-point extension"
  default y if RV64
  default n

config RV_D
  bool "D: double-precision floating-point extension"
  depends on RV_F
  default y if RV64
  default n

config RV_SVADE
  bool "Svade: A/D bits faulted by hardware (instead of Svadu auto-update)"
  default y
  help
    Match the Raptor HDL page-table walker: an access with PTE.A=0, or a
    store with PTE.D=0, raises a page fault and never updates the PTE in
    hardware. Disable only when intentionally modeling a Svadu target.

config RV_RVA22S64
  bool "RVA22S64 architectural execution environment"
  depends on RV64 && RV_F && RV_D && RV_SVADE
  default y
  help
    Enable the RVA22S64 execution environment by default for RV64, matching
    the default RV64 RTL configuration.

config RV_MCOUNTINHIBIT
  bool "Optional mcountinhibit CSR (read-only zero)"
  default y if RV_RVA22S64
  default n
  help
    Expose the optional mcountinhibit CSR as read-only zero so firmware
    such as OpenSBI can discover privileged architecture 1.12 through
    mcounteren, mcountinhibit and menvcfg. Counters always run.
    Disable when using NEMU as a reference for a core without this CSR,
    including the current Raptor RTL. This is independent of RVA22S64.

config RV_EBREAK_HOST_EXIT
  bool "Legacy EBREAK host-exit convention"
  depends on DEBUG
  default y if !RV64
  default n
  help
    Treat EBREAK (including C.EBREAK) as a host test exit using a0,
    except while signature testing. Enable for legacy AM/test payloads
    that use this convention. Otherwise EBREAK raises a guest breakpoint
    exception, including in debug builds. Independent of ISA support.
endmenu
